  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Reduction of  TB prevalence by 6 % by 2017 - Sao Tome and Principe (01-Jul-2015-31-Dec-2017)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sao Tome and Principe, Tuberculosis, United Nations Development Programme (UNDP Sao Tome and Principe)This program has the following goals: Ending the Tuberculosis epidemic in Sao Tome and Principe by 2035. The objectives of this program are: Increase TB case notification rates from 71 cases / 100,000 inhabitants in 2012 to 80 cases / 100,000 in 2017 through increased screening among key populations.  Increase TB treatment success rates to more than 85%, by putting the emphasis on rigorous directly observed treatment (DOTs).  Provide care and support to more than 95% of TB/HIV co-infected patients through HIV testing of more than 95% of TB patients; TB screening for all PLHIV; and treatment provision (Cotrimoxazole, ART) to TB/HIV;.  Provide routine screening of resistance through Xpert test in all TB cases and the treatment of MDR-TB.  To improve the managerial capacity of the National Tuberculosis Programme (PNLT)</narrative>
  </description>
